{"id":"wikibooks:chicken-marinade","verdict":"keep","recipes":[{"source":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook%3AChicken_Marinade","status":"fixed","reason":"restore quantities lost from conversion templates","ingredients":["½ cup (125 ml) chicken broth","¾ cup (185 ml) white wine","2 tbsp Worcestershire sauce","2 tbsp lemon pepper","3 tbsp cayenne pepper","¼ cup (85 g) honey","2 tbsp minced garlic","3 sprigs rosemary, finely chopped","¼ cup (60 ml) extra-virgin olive oil","1 tbsp finely grated lemon zest","10 sprigs thyme, finely chopped","2 tbsp salt","2 tbsp black pepper"],"steps":["Combine all ingredients in a gallon size zip-top bag.","Refrigerate for up to 2 weeks before using to marinate chicken.","To use, proceed as directed in given recipe OR submerge chicken in marinade and let rest for several hours in the fridge before cooking."]}]}
